IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cha-ipc-regulations`

-- Charities (Institutions of a Public Character) Regulations (Cap. 37, Rg 5) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, the Commissioner's guidance or a Sector Administrator's practice.
--
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text of ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1994-RG5.txt.

-- A test helper: an applicant that meets every reg 3(1) condition except as the arguments say.
GIVEN `registered or exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits the community as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `board size` IS A NUMBER
      `independent members` IS A NUMBER
      `citizen members` IS A NUMBER
      `waiver of (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `waiver of (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `waiver of (ea)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IPC applicant`
`an applicant with` MEANS
    `IPC applicant` WITH
        `is a registered or exempt charity in Singapore` IS `registered or exempt`,
        `governing instruments approved by the Sector Administrator` IS TRUE,
        `activities exclusively beneficial to the community in Singapore as a whole` IS `benefits the community as a whole`,
        `activities meet its objectives and the Sector Administrator's objectives` IS TRUE,
        `number of governing board members` IS `board size`,
        `number of board members not caught by reg 3(4)(a) to (d)` IS `independent members`,
        `number of board members who are Singapore citizens` IS `citizen members`,
        `board accountable for the management of donations` IS TRUE,
        `auditor's appointment approved by the Sector Administrator` IS TRUE,
        `approval not contrary to the public interest` IS TRUE,
        `condition (c) waived by the Minister` IS `waiver of (c)`,
        `condition (ea) waived by the Minister` IS `waiver of (ea)`,
        `condition (e) waived by the Commissioner` IS `waiver of (e)`

-- The Haziq charity (assumed facts): newly registered, board of 8 of whom 4 are independent in the reg 3(4) sense and 4 are
-- citizens, open to the whole community, governing instruments and auditor approved, no waivers.
GIVETH AN `IPC applicant`
`the newly registered charity` MEANS `an applicant with` TRUE TRUE 8 4 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `REQ-0292 (Haziq scenario h072) -- on what conditions`

-- Who decides: the Sector Administrator of its sector, or the Commissioner where none is designated (reg 2). Not the Comptroller.
#ASSERT `who decides an IPC application` FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner of Charities`
#ASSERT `who decides an IPC application` TRUE EQUALS `the Sector Administrator designated for the sector`
#ASSERT NOT (`who decides an IPC application` FALSE EQUALS `the Comptroller of Income Tax as decision maker`)

-- On the facts it meets every reg 3(1) condition (exactly half the board independent and citizens is enough), so it may be
-- approved -- but approval is not a right: reg 4(2) lets the decision maker refuse anyway.
#ASSERT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` `the newly registered charity`
#ASSERT `the outcome open on a first application` `the newly registered charity` EQUALS `may be approved, but the Sector Administrator may still refuse under reg 4(2)`

-- A first approval lasts at most 2 years (reg 4(3)); an approval specified as 3 years is read as 2.
#ASSERT `the longest first approval in years` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the period of a first approval in years` 3 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the period of a first approval in years` 1 EQUALS 1

-- Only while approval is current, and only for a donation that is tax deductible under the Income Tax Act, may it issue a tax
-- deduction receipt (regs 9(1), 9(7)). Before approval it may not.
#ASSERT `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` `approval current` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` `never approved` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` `approval current` FALSE

§ `reg 3 -- conditions and the reg 5A waivers`

-- (a) cannot be waived: an unregistered charity cannot be approved.
#ASSERT `the outcome open on a first application` (`an applicant with` FALSE TRUE 8 4 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `cannot be approved`
#ASSERT `who may waive under reg 5A` `condition (a) registered or exempt charity` EQUALS `no one may waive it`

-- (e) independence: 3 of 8 fails (6 < 8); the Commissioner's waiver cures it.
#ASSERT NOT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE TRUE 8 3 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE TRUE 8 3 4 FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `who may waive under reg 5A` `condition (e) independent board` EQUALS `the Commissioner may waive it`

-- (ea) citizens: 3 of 8 fails; the Minister's waiver cures it. 4 of 7 passes (8 >= 7).
#ASSERT NOT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE TRUE 8 4 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE TRUE 8 4 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `at least half the board are Singapore citizens` 7 4
#ASSERT `who may waive under reg 5A` `condition (ea) half the board citizens` EQUALS `the Minister may waive it`

-- (c) a charity confined to one religious group fails; the Minister may waive.
#ASSERT NOT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE FALSE 8 4 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` (`an applicant with` TRUE FALSE 8 4 4 TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `who may waive under reg 5A` `condition (c) benefit to the community as a whole` EQUALS `the Minister may waive it`
#ASSERT `who may waive under reg 5A` `condition (g) auditor approved` EQUALS `no one may waive it`

-- The reg 3(7) Illustration: a board of 7, of whom A, B, C, D are related to each other, leaves 3 not caught -- fails (6 < 7).
#ASSERT NOT `the independence requirement in reg 3(4) is met` 7 3

-- reg 3(5): a spouse's sibling is related; a cousin and a sibling's spouse are not.
#ASSERT `is related under reg 3(5)` `spouse's sibling`
#ASSERT `is related under reg 3(5)` `grandparent`
#ASSERT NOT `is related under reg 3(5)` `cousin`
#ASSERT NOT `is related under reg 3(5)` `sibling's spouse`

§ `reg 5 -- extension`

#ASSERT `the extension application is in time under reg 5(2)` 2 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the extension application is in time under reg 5(2)` 1 FALSE
#ASSERT `the extension application is in time under reg 5(2)` 1 TRUE
#ASSERT `the longest extension in years` EQUALS 5

§ `reg 6 -- suspension and revocation, and what it does to donations`

#ASSERT `the position under reg 6` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Sector Administrator must revoke`
#ASSERT `the position under reg 6` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Sector Administrator may suspend for up to 2 years or revoke`
#ASSERT `the position under reg 6` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no ground under reg 6`
#ASSERT `donations made in this state are kept out of tax deduction by reg 6(3)(a)` `approval suspended`
#ASSERT NOT `donations made in this state are kept out of tax deduction by reg 6(3)(a)` `approval current`
#ASSERT `the donation must be refunded in full under reg 6(3)(c)` `approval revoked` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the donation must be refunded in full under reg 6(3)(c)` `approval revoked` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` `approval expired` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` `approval suspended` TRUE

§ `regs 9 and 10 -- receipts and donation records`

#ASSERT `the receipt has the reg 9(3) contents` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the receipt has the reg 9(3) contents` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the receipt has the reg 9(3) contents` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the donation record has every reg 10(2) particular` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the donation record has every reg 10(2) particular` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Year of assessment 2052: kept to the end of 2057.
#ASSERT `the record must be kept to the end of` 2052 EQUALS 2057
-- INFERRED year of assessment for a donation received in 2051 is 2052, so to the end of 2057.
#ASSERT `the record must be kept to the end of` (`the inferred year of assessment for a donation received in` 2051) EQUALS 2057

§ `reg 11 -- use of donations`

#ASSERT `the use permitted by reg 11` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the purpose the donor specified`
#ASSERT `the use permitted by reg 11` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the purpose communicated to the donor`
#ASSERT `the use permitted by reg 11` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `any activity of the institution`
#ASSERT `the use permitted by reg 11` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `refund within 4 years or another purpose the Sector Administrator approves`

§ `regs 15, 16, 17(7), 20`

-- Inferred formula: expenses 30,000 against receipts 90,000 and sponsorships 10,000 -> cap 30,000, within; 30,001 is not.
#ASSERT `within the reg 15 cap on the inferred formula` 30000 90000 10000
#ASSERT NOT `within the reg 15 cap on the inferred formula` 30001 90000 10000
#ASSERT `the year by whose 31 January the Comptroller must have the details` 2051 EQUALS 2052
#ASSERT `months after the financial year end to furnish reg 16(1) documents` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the auditor must be changed under reg 17(7)` 5
#ASSERT NOT `the auditor must be changed under reg 17(7)` 4
#ASSERT `is a large IPC under reg 20(6)` 10000000 12000000
#ASSERT NOT `is a large IPC under reg 20(6)` 9999999 12000000
#ASSERT NOT `meets the reg 20(2) board size` 10000000 10000000 9 FALSE
#ASSERT `meets the reg 20(2) board size` 9000000 10000000 9 FALSE

§ `regs 21 and 22 -- offences and penalty`

#ASSERT `the consequence of contravening` `reg 10 donation records` EQUALS `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
#ASSERT `the consequence of contravening` `reg 11(8) telling the Comptroller of a refund` EQUALS `no offence or penalty in Part VI`
#ASSERT `the consequence of contravening` `reg 16(2)(a) donation details to the Comptroller` EQUALS `no offence or penalty in Part VI`
#ASSERT `the consequence of contravening` `reg 15(1) fund-raising expenses` EQUALS `offence under reg 21(2), no continuing-offence fine`
#ASSERT `the consequence of contravening` `reg 9(7) receipt after expiry, suspension or revocation` EQUALS `financial penalty under reg 22`
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under reg 21(1)` 10 EQUALS 11000
-- 0.4 x 50,000 = 20,000; 0.4 x 200 = 80, so the $100 floor applies.
#ASSERT `the reg 22 financial penalty` 50000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the reg 22 financial penalty` 200 EQUALS 100
